From c4f0b39e0c0f068e5e545b7a9c3271d4cf857de6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hemant Kumar <heman10x@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 21:16:34 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] local: add moe-trace tool and an env gate for mmap
 prefetch

Local research fork only. Not for upstream, no PR intended.

moe-trace dumps MoE routing decisions (selected expert id and normalized gate
weight) for every token of a prefill pass, one CSV row per token/layer/slot, via
the eval callback on ffn_moe_topk. Layer index is parsed back out of the tensor
name rather than tracked with a counter, so it stays exact when some layers are
dense. It appends per layer across micro-batches instead of overwriting, because
a prompt longer than the micro-batch is prefilled in several llama_decode calls
and overwriting would silently keep only the last chunk.

This is what produced the routing measurements the streaming design rests on:
220 tokens, 56,760 accesses, 88.9% of expert accesses being repeats.

llama-model.cpp gates init_mappings prefetch behind LLAMA_NO_PREFETCH. Prefetch
faults in the whole mapping, which is fatal when the model is 82.5 GB and the
machine has 15.4 GB. Note the experiment did NOT support the hypothesis:
disabling prefetch made the run die sooner (26 s vs 66 s), so this is kept as an
env-gated no-op and is explicitly not upstream-worthy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
